# Agda scratch probes.  Agents testing whether something reduces on the nose
# write throwaway modules; two of these (`ZZTestSolver.agda`, `Probe1.agda`)
# were swept into commits by `git add -A` and had to be removed again.  A
# probe is a question, not a result: name it `Probe*.agda` or `Scratch*.agda`
# and it stays out of the tree.  Anything worth keeping goes in
# `NaturalMachine/` under a name that carries its category.
formal/cubical/Probe*.agda
formal/cubical/Tmp*.agda
formal/cubical/**/Tmp*.agda
formal/cubical/Scratch*.agda
formal/cubical/**/Probe*.agda
formal/cubical/**/Scratch*.agda
runtime/LIVING_RUN.log
runtime/LIVING_STATE.json
vigil-state.json
natural_machine_cpu_loop_rust/real_workload
natural_machine_cpu_loop_rust/decic_extend
natural_machine_cpu_loop_rust/root_singular_series
formal/cubical/Candidate_*.agda

# machine/library.terms is NOT ignored, and used to be, listed right here
# among the reproducible artifacts.  It is the opposite of one: it is the
# machine's MEMORY, the file MathMachine reads at startup to re-admit what
# earlier runs proved.  Ignored, it never left the container that wrote it,
# so every fresh checkout — every CI job, every new session, every future
# scheduled run — started the machine from mRules = [] and re-derived the
# same theorems forever.  The engine's own comment says the architecture
# "rests on installed theorems compounding"; nothing can compound across a
# clone that does not carry the file.  Tracked as of 2026-08-17.

# Machine build artifacts (reproducible; never source of truth)
machine/*.hi
machine/*.o
machine/arithvocab
machine/bench-head-depth
machine/cyclotomic-vocab
machine/parallel-gate
machine/library.certs
machine/self_architecture.tsv
machine/nested-agda/

# Certificate gate cache: re-derivable, and every entry stores the exact
# module source it certified, so it is a rebuildable artifact not a record.
machine/.certcache/
formal/cubical/.claude/
machine/replay.traces.live

# The sabhā: the compiled process and its transcript.  The binary is
# rebuildable from machine/check-sabha.sh; the transcript is a session
# record, kept locally and never rewritten in place (append-only), and it
# is the corpus this wire exists to produce.
machine/sabha
machine/sabha.jsonl

# The interface the other carrier is handed: the compiled binary, rebuildable
# from machine/check-karana.sh.  Its outputs (the tool schema, the training
# records) are regenerated from the running dispatch table and a transcript,
# so neither is committed either -- a committed copy would be the second copy
# that drifts, which is the thing this lane exists to remove.
machine/karana
machine/abhyasa.jsonl
**/.certcache/

# compiled binaries — build output, rebuilt in place by machine/check-*.sh; never track
machine/math-machine
machine/repairfixpoint
machine/question-machine

# the supervised loop's runtime traces (phase_keep commits the report when it lands; the log and tmp are breath, not body)
collab/orchestration/machine-loop.log
machine/sanghatta-report-current.txt.tmp
